/target
/.crush
/.idea
/tmp
# R6-OPT-A6: per-run raw provenance dumps from scripts/paired-ab-runner.mjs --
# generated output, accumulates one timestamped JSON per invocation, not source.
# SAME scratch-by-default / `git add -f`-when-cited policy as `_raw_*.log`
# below: some reports (R31_10 §5.2, R32-0/c72a27b, R32-12/e88390b) force-add
# specific paired_ab_runs JSON filenames as their cited provenance, and 33 such
# files remain tracked across rounds 14-32. R33-5 (task #510) deliberately chose
# the curated `_raw_*.log` route instead (truncatable per R14-10, reproducible)
# -- both are legitimate citation homes; this bare ignore line previously
# lacked the exception clause `_raw_*.log` already documents (R34-1/task #520).
/docs/perf/paired_ab_runs/
# R13-10 (task #280): scratch raw command-output logs from bench/test/iai
# sweeps (`docs/perf/_raw_*.log`) are throwaway by default -- ignored so ad-hoc
# local runs never accumulate as untracked noise (22 such files had piled up
# across R9-R11 before this rule). EXCEPTION: when a perf-gate report in
# docs/perf/*.md cites specific `_raw_*.log` filenames as its evidence (the
# R13-6/R13-8/R13-9 gate docs already do this), `git add -f` those specific
# files so the cited evidence is reproducible from the commit, not just from
# a re-run. Do not `git add -f` logs a doc does not name.
/docs/perf/_raw_*.log
# task #493: scripts/capture-measurement-identity.mjs --patch-hash now saves
# the patch it hashes to docs/perf/_raw_identity_<tree-sha-prefix>.patch --
# same "scratch by default, git add -f only when a report cites it" policy
# as the _raw_*.log rule immediately above.
/docs/perf/_raw_identity_*.patch
